u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into the {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-2}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into {{field-4}} ." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311739 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4ee21254-0061-505a-86c2-50174dc611d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311739 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L2},$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Let's substitute ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$ from $\\text{L1}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ into the initial system of ODEs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =Ax(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t) & =AΦu(t)+f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into $\\text{initial system of ODEs}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are linearly independent. So, $Φ$ is invertible. Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{pre-multiplying by }{Φ}^{-1}$ both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ ({Φ}^{-1}Φ)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L7},$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Substituting\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φu(t) \\\\  & =Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into  $\\text{L1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365599 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365599 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365599 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365599 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186365600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365599 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2b0824a7-3977-53c2-8ae9-fab24fac62a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365600 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365600 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365600 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "eabf843f-76af-5374-87f3-015cd7c21177" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365601 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365601 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186482873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365601 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365601 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365601 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186482873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365601 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e2490d5f-d96a-5160-b6f7-a7d11c4a92d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365602 #edb/ref 1080 "-4{e}^{-4t}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365602 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365602 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e7d357d-8554-535e-9625-2f454e5a740e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186496829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [